<speak>The dining area is quiet today. My husband is out meeting an old school friend, and the grandchildren are not visiting until the weekend. Usually the table has colouring books at one end and somebody's water bottle at the other. I cleared it this morning, which felt quite satisfying. There is still a little basket of crayons on the sideboard, though. I have learned not to put everything away too thoroughly, otherwise we spend the next visit looking for it all again.</speak>